Z||000000||87GTZ34||01-26-2001||03:36 PM||||Does anyone know if GM wired in the cruise in the steering column and in the body to console & back where the solenoid & servo are?  I have and '87 GM manual & it shows the harness in the rear compt but doesn't specify that it is an option.  The manual also doesn't show the console harness where the cruise module plugs in or the turn stalk or the brake switch connector.<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||01-26-2001||04:25 PM||||87GTZ34,<P>I'm having a little problem trying to follow your question(s) but I'll try:<P>The cruise control stalk is a seperate wire that runs down your steering column. Most any year GM stalk that looks simular will work if your needs replacing. The cruise control module is located behind the carpet on the tunnel in front of your right knee. To the best of my knowledge, the harnes exits through the firewall in the center, the same place as the engine harness. For troubleshooting try this link:http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html<P>Hope this helps,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000002||87GTZ34||01-26-2001||05:03 PM||||Okay let me clarify.  Does any Fiero w/o factory equipped cruise, have the wiring built into the body of the car?  <P>Or did they have variations of variations of wiring harnesses based on options.  cruise/no cruise - pwr mir/no pwr mir - AC/no AC etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-26-2001||07:57 PM||||That I can tell.... I think this depends on engine and year. I've only verified it for 87-88 4 cyl so far. these ECM's have the cruise built in, unlike the others that require a seperate module.<P>cruise is what I call an over lay item. There is, at least in some versions, a separate harness that is layed in with the main harness at build time.<P>If you are looking to add cruise the best thing is to use an after market one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||01-26-2001||09:14 PM||||Thanks ogre.  That is what I figured.  I am actually selling my cruise minus the turn stalk.  I'm putting a '96 cruise setup from the Z34 in and selling the orignal Fiero setup.  I just want to let the buyer know what they're in for.<P>thanks again <p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
